WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.712
Start with the simplest architecture that solves the problem.

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:08.777
If every step is already known, use a fixed Python workflow.

00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:15.102
It will usually be easier to test, faster to run, and easier to explain.

00:00:15.102 --> 00:00:21.187
If the main problem is finding information in documents, classic rag may be enough.

00:00:21.766 --> 00:00:30.178
Use an agent when the next action genuinely depends on runtime observations and several approved tools may be needed.

00:00:30.178 --> 00:00:37.773
Use agentic rag when retrieval itself can fail, require grading, need query rewriting,

00:00:37.773 --> 00:00:41.073
or require evidence from multiple sources.

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:50.313
Use Lang Graph when state, branching, loops, persistence, approval, or resumable execution need to be explicit.

00:00:50.763 --> 00:00:54.845
Do not choose architecture because one framework is fashionable.

00:00:54.845 --> 00:00:59.809
Choose it because the uncertainty in the workflow requires that level of control.
